### Book Leaf Register API
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Click "Send Request" above any block below.
###
### Routes are defined in routes/api.php and mounted under the "api" prefix
### by App\Providers\RouteServiceProvider (Route::prefix('api')->group(...)).
### Auth is Laravel Sanctum: POST /api/auth/login returns a bearer token,
### which must be sent as "Authorization: Bearer <token>" on protected routes.

# @baseUrl = http://localhost/appuser/public/api
@baseUrl = http://appuser.templesoftware.in/public/api

### Fill these in with real values from your local `users` table
### before running the Login request.
@email = hari@punnyam.com
@password = 12345678


### 1. Login — get a Sanctum token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 2. List counters (requires a valid token from the login response above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/counters
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 3. List poojas for a deity
POST {{baseUrl}}/deity/poojas
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deity": 1
}


### 4. List deities
GET {{baseUrl}}/deities
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 5. List stars
GET {{baseUrl}}/stars
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### --- Book Leaf Register ---

### Fill in a real pooja_id from GET/POST poojas for this tenant before running these.
@poojaId = 138

### 6. Register a new book batch (leaf 1-40, 4 leaves/book → 10 books)
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "pooja_id": {{poojaId}},
  "leaf_from": 1,
  "leaf_to": 40,
  "leafs_per_book": 10
}


### 7. List book batches (paginated, default 10/page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 8. List book batches, page 2, 5 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/book-register?per_page=5&page=2
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 9. List book batches filtered by date and pooja
GET {{baseUrl}}/book-register?date=2026-07-20&pooja_id={{poojaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### Fill in a real counter_id (see request 2 above) and book_id (see request 10 below).
@counterId = 1
@bookId = 11
@poojaId = 102

### 10. List books available to issue for a pooja (next starting leaf pre-filled)
# @name availableBooks
GET {{baseUrl}}/book-issue/available?pooja_id={{poojaId}}&counter_id={{counterId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 11. Issue a book to a counter (counter_id is per-item since each pooja can go to a different counter)
# @name issueBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-issue
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "items": [
    { "pooja_id": {{poojaId}}, "book_id": {{bookId}}, "counter_id": {{counterId}}, "leaf_from": 1 }
  ]
}


### 12. List open book issues for a counter (Close & Settle screen)
GET {{baseUrl}}/book-issue?date=2026-07-20&counter_id={{counterId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### Fill in the book_issue_id from request 11's response (data[0].id).
@bookIssueId = 1

### 13. Settle a book issue (record last leaf used)
# @name settleBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-settlement
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "counter_id": {{counterId}},
  "items": [
    { "book_issue_id": {{bookIssueId}}, "leaf_used_to": 4 }
  ]
}


### 13b. Correct a settlement (e.g. staff mis-entered leaf_used_to earlier).
### {{settleBook.response.body.data[0].id}} is the book_settlement.id, NOT book_issue_id.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/book-settlement/{{settleBook.response.body.data[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leaf_used_to": 3
}


### --- Book Leaf Register Reports ---
### These are read-only; run after the happy path above so there's data to report on.

@fromDate = 2026-07-01
@toDate = 2026-07-31

### 13c. Book register list — batches registered for a pooja, in a date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-register?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}&pooja_id={{poojaId}}&per_page=15
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13d. Book register summary — totals per pooja (batches, leaves, books) in range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-register-summary?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13e. Book issue list — narrow to one counter + pooja (cheap, recommended for drill-down)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-issue?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}&pooja_id={{poojaId}}&counter_id={{counterId}}&per_page=15
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13f. Book issue list — wide date range, no counter (heavier: every counter's rows, paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-issue?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13g. Book issue list — filter to only still-open (unsettled) issues
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-issue?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}&status=open
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13h. Book issue summary — counter-wise: issued/open/settled counts per counter in range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-issue-summary?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13i. Book issue summary — narrowed to one pooja, still grouped by counter
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-issue-summary?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}&pooja_id={{poojaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13j. Book settlement list — narrow to one counter + pooja
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-settlement?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}&pooja_id={{poojaId}}&counter_id={{counterId}}&per_page=15
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13k. Book settlement summary — counter-wise leaves consumed in range
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/book-settlement-summary?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13l. Counter statement — single endpoint: everything for one counter, one date range
### (totals + pooja-wise breakdown + paginated issue/settlement detail rows)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/counter-statement?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}&counter_id={{counterId}}&per_page=15
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 13m. Counter statement without counter_id → expect 422 (counter_id is required here)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/counter-statement?from_date={{fromDate}}&to_date={{toDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### 14. Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### =====================================================================
### --- Failure cases worth trying (run after the happy path above) ---
### =====================================================================

### 15. Missing token → expect 401 Unauthenticated
POST {{baseUrl}}/counters


### 16. Garbage token → expect 401 Unauthenticated
POST {{baseUrl}}/counters
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token


### 17. Login with wrong password → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "definitely-wrong"
}


### 18. Login missing password → expect 401 validation error
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}


### 19. Register with leaf_to less than leaf_from → expect 422 validation error
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "pooja_id": {{poojaId}},
  "leaf_from": 40,
  "leaf_to": 1,
  "leafs_per_book": 4
}


### 20. Register with a leaf range that doesn't divide evenly → expect 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "pooja_id": {{poojaId}},
  "leaf_from": 1,
  "leaf_to": 41,
  "leafs_per_book": 4
}


### 20b. Register a leaf range that overlaps an existing batch for the same pooja → expect 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "pooja_id": {{poojaId}},
  "leaf_from": 20,
  "leaf_to": 60,
  "leafs_per_book": 4
}


### 21. Register missing required fields → expect 422 with first validation message
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20"
}


### 22. Register without a token → expect 401 Unauthenticated
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "pooja_id": {{poojaId}},
  "leaf_from": 1,
  "leaf_to": 40,
  "leafs_per_book": 4
}


### 23. Issue a book that's already open → expect 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-issue
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "items": [
    { "pooja_id": {{poojaId}}, "book_id": {{bookId}}, "counter_id": {{counterId}}, "leaf_from": 1 }
  ]
}


### 23b. Issue a book with a wrong leaf_from (not matching the next expected leaf) → expect 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-issue
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-21",
  "items": [
    { "pooja_id": {{poojaId}}, "book_id": {{bookId}}, "counter_id": {{counterId}}, "leaf_from": 1 }
  ]
}


### 24. Issue missing items → expect 422 validation error
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-issue
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20"
}


### 25. Settle with leaf_used_to beyond the book's leaf range → expect 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-settlement
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "counter_id": {{counterId}},
  "items": [
    { "book_issue_id": {{bookIssueId}}, "leaf_used_to": 9999 }
  ]
}


### 26. Settle an already-settled book issue → expect 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/book-settlement
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-07-20",
  "counter_id": {{counterId}},
  "items": [
    { "book_issue_id": {{bookIssueId}}, "leaf_used_to": 4 }
  ]
}


### 27. Correct a settlement with leaf_used_to beyond the book's leaf range → expect 422
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/book-settlement/{{settleBook.response.body.data[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leaf_used_to": 9999
}


### 28. Correct a non-existent settlement id → expect 422
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/book-settlement/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "leaf_used_to": 3
}
